Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_enable
Type: boolean
Default: true
Description: Configure a dedicated SendmailAnalyzer web subdomain?
 SendmailAnalyzer can publish its local PSGI service through a dedicated
 HTTPS Apache VirtualHost such as reports.example.test.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_domain
Type: string
Description: Existing DNS domain for the SendmailAnalyzer site:
 Enter the existing base domain under which the reporting subdomain should
 be created, for example example.test.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_subdomain
Type: string
Default: reports
Description: SendmailAnalyzer reporting subdomain:
 This label is combined with the existing domain. The default creates a host
 such as reports.example.test.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_address
Type: string
Description: IPv4 address for the reporting subdomain:
 When the selected domain is hosted by a local authoritative BIND zone,
 SendmailAnalyzer can add this A record transactionally.
 .
 If DNS is hosted elsewhere, this value is still used to document the
 external A record that should exist.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_username
Type: string
Default: sendmailreports
Description: Username for Internet access:
 Localhost and the configured LAN may access the reporting site directly.
 Other clients must authenticate with this username.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_lan
Type: string
Description: LAN network allowed without a password:
 Enter one IPv4 CIDR such as 192.0.2.0/24.
 .
 Localhost is always allowed. Leave this empty if no LAN bypass is wanted.

Template: sendmailanalyzer/site_password
Type: password
Description: Password for Internet access:
 Enter the password for the reporting-site Basic Auth account.
 .
 The clear-text value is used only to create a bcrypt htpasswd hash and is
 cleared from the package configuration database after installation.
